1
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,510
Leo is making party bags.

2
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,720
He has 24 sweets and 36 stickers.

3
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:16,590
Every bag must be exactly the same, and nothing can be left over.

4
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:19,830
What is the greatest number of bags he can make?

5
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:23,380
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:29,650
The number of bags must divide 24 exactly, and it must divide 36 exactly.

7
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:30,580
12 works.

8
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:36,230
24 divided by 12 is 2, and 36 divided by 12 is 3.

9
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:40,760
So Leo can make 12 bags, each with 2 sweets and 3 stickers.

10
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:43,610
No bigger number divides both.

11
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,270
A factor of a number divides it exactly.

12
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,290
Factors come in pairs.

13
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:54,560
24 is 1 times 24, 2 times 12, 3 times 8, and 4 times 6.

14
00:00:54,610 --> 00:01:00,650
So the factors of 24 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12 and 24.

15
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,660
A common factor divides both numbers.

16
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:06,900
Compare the factors of 24 and 36.

17
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:11,480
The common factors are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 12.

18
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:13,080
The biggest one is 12.

19
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:16,890
We call it the highest common factor, or HCF.

20
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,390
Here is a quicker way.

21
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:23,590
Take the smaller number, and test its factors from the biggest down.

22
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:25,800
Find the HCF of 18 and 45.

23
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:27,920
The smaller number is 18.

24
00:01:27,970 --> 00:01:32,630
Its factors from the top are 18, 9, 6, and so on.

25
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,330
Does 18 divide 45?

26
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:34,620
No.

27
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:36,230
Does 9 divide 45?

28
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:38,700
Yes, 45 divided by 9 is 5.

29
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:40,760
So the HCF is 9.

30
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:41,540
Your turn.

31
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:43,560
Find the HCF of 12 and 18.

32
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:47,060
Pause the video and try it.

33
00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:49,320
The smaller number is 12.

34
00:01:49,370 --> 00:01:50,950
Does 12 divide 18?

35
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,220
No.

36
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:52,580
Next factor, 6.

37
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:54,480
18 divided by 6 is 3.

38
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:56,480
So the HCF is 6.

39
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:57,810
Here is the method.

40
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:01,650
Step 1: list the factors of the smaller number.

41
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:07,590
Step 2: start with the biggest, and test whether it divides the other number.

42
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:11,250
Step 3: the first one that works is the HCF.

43
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:15,350
Remember, the HCF is never bigger than the smaller number.

44
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:18,300
And if only 1 works, the HCF is 1.

45
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:21,390
Find the HCF of 28 and 42.

46
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:27,680
Use factor pairs for 28: 1 times 28, 2 times 14, 4 times 7.

47
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,750
Test from the biggest.

48
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,810
28 does not divide 42.

49
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:34,720
14 does: 42 divided by 14 is 3.

50
00:02:34,770 --> 00:02:36,580
The HCF is 14.

51
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:39,860
Sometimes the only common factor is 1.

52
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:43,560
For 8 and 15, none of 8, 4 or 2 divides 15.

53
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:45,490
So the HCF is 1.

54
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:48,130
Find the HCF of 30, 45 and 60.

55
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,360
Work in two stages.

56
00:02:50,410 --> 00:02:52,090
First, 30 and 45.

57
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:55,660
30 does not divide 45, but 15 does.

58
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:57,840
Their HCF is 15.

59
00:02:57,890 --> 00:02:59,320
Now 15 and 60.

60
00:02:59,370 --> 00:03:04,950
60 divided by 15 is 4, so 15 divides 60 as well.

61
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,990
The HCF of 30, 45 and 60 is 15.

62
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:09,850
Your turn.

63
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:12,420
Find the HCF of 20, 30 and 50.

64
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:15,700
Pause and work it out.

65
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:20,710
For 20 and 30: 20 does not divide 30, but 10 does.

66
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,410
Then 50 divided by 10 is 5.

67
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,660
So the HCF is 10.

68
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:29,100
A floor is 120 centimetres by 84 centimetres.

69
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:34,700
We want equal square tiles, as large as possible, with no cutting.

70
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:38,380
The side of a tile must divide both 120 and 84.

71
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:41,660
As large as possible means the HCF.

72
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:47,560
Test the factors of 84 from the top: 84, 42, 28, 21, 14.

73
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:50,190
None of them divides 120.

74
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:54,640
But 12 does: 120 divided by 12 is 10.

75
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:57,460
So each tile is 12 centimetres wide.

76
00:03:57,510 --> 00:04:01,860
The floor takes 10 tiles one way and 7 the other.

77
00:04:01,910 --> 00:04:04,450
Omar wants the HCF of 12 and 30.

78
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:07,260
Which line goes wrong first?

79
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:08,580
Line 2 is wrong.

80
00:04:08,630 --> 00:04:09,730
Omar missed 6.

81
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:14,380
30 divided by 6 is 5, so 6 is a common factor too.

82
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:17,350
The common factors are 1, 2, 3 and 6.

83
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:19,180
So the HCF is 6.

84
00:04:19,230 --> 00:04:21,330
This video is in Full HD.

85
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:27,390
That means the picture is 1920 pixels wide and 1080 pixels high.

86
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:30,720
The HCF of 1920 and 1080 is 120.

87
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:33,970
Divide both numbers by it.

88
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,250
You get 16 and 9.

89
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:40,190
That is why people call this screen shape sixteen by nine.

90
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,620
One last question.

91
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:43,680
Find the HCF of 27 and 63.

92
00:04:43,730 --> 00:04:47,220
Pause the video and answer.

93
00:04:47,270 --> 00:04:51,360
The factors of 27 from the top are 27, then 9.

94
00:04:51,410 --> 00:04:53,340
27 does not divide 63.

95
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:55,950
9 does: 63 divided by 9 is 7.

96
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,930
So the HCF is 9.

97
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:01,390
To remember: a common factor divides both numbers.

98
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:03,810
The HCF is the biggest one.

99
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:08,330
Test the factors of the smaller number, from the top down.

100
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:12,590
The HCF is at most the smaller number, and at least 1.

101
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:18,700
Problems about the largest equal groups, or the biggest equal tiles, use the HCF.

102
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:23,870
Great work! Now practise lesson 1.4 on Camday.
